      "body": "No actionable source or contract findings emitted. Bounded native semantic review passed; **REVIEW_INCOMPLETE for merge readiness** pending protected integration/hosted qualification. Keep Draft.\n\nreviewed_head_sha: `67dc5af9a15590fc8476d09217232831a0009952`\nintegration_basis: candidate basis `d08c77d144c016078364fcc1fcf2fa593d21cefc`; observed PR base `e660a99480dc13a4ed93b131042d11506fd484b6`. No combined-tree qualification claimed.\nclaim_boundary: #8210 selected-partition disclosure in native JSON/human; #8201 retains fanout ownership.\n\nInspected all seven changed files and followed the producer into actual consumers: Rust partial scope -> preview dispatch -> normalized selects predicate -> detect_preview_advisories -> analyzed helper -> JSON/human renderers. Enabled source advisories now share dispatch's selected-path authority. Disabled presence and missing-source/exclusion handling remain; Perl's supplied packet scope is explicitly excluded from the new filter. No classifier, partition, exit, DTO, support-tier or gate-policy change. Spec/schema/traceability/test admission agree.\n\nObserved independent proof: exact-head detached checkout, Rust/Cargo 1.95.0, Linux x86_64/default features; native build exit0; 2 partial_preview_disclosure tests passed (532 filtered out), 4 unsupported_check_exit tests passed (530 filtered out). A separate harness's final **24 native invocations** parse complete JSON bytes and inspect human output for both Python and TypeScript: omitted/partly-selected/full/disabled controls, literal paths/counts/samples, nonempty Rust/preview subjects, raw input totals, partial/non-consumable/gate-ineligible state, enablement guidance and exit0. Mixed malformed inputs retain Rust findings, disclose unsupported_input/incomplete and exit2 in both projections. Final selected Cargo test-built executable SHA256 `8c8fd43cd63323e92f65440a2264ef0793a6fc307c617b83f1d1a49cc4ac9b9c`.\n\nOracle challenge: selected/full controls reject deleting all or all partial advisories; disabled controls reject losing presence guidance; literal samples reject count-only repair; partial and malformed controls reject false completeness/exit promotion. Retained pre-repair logs were inspected and show both omitted-advisory assertions rejecting old production. Those red logs are historical author evidence, not an independently executed red run. No source mutation experiment was made under the no-source-changes instruction.\n\nDurable [inspection record and raw evidence](https://github.com/EffortlessMetrics/ripr-swarm/blob/ae7bbaa32fb7190800fd0deb439868443ad60f07/README.md), [24-invocation receipt with exact argv/env/config/diff bytes and stream hashes](https://github.com/EffortlessMetrics/ripr-swarm/blob/ae7bbaa32fb7190800fd0deb439868443ad60f07/native-receipt.json), [terminal validation](https://github.com/EffortlessMetrics/ripr-swarm/blob/ae7bbaa32fb7190800fd0deb439868443ad60f07/validation.json), and [manifest](https://github.com/EffortlessMetrics/ripr-swarm/blob/ae7bbaa32fb7190800fd0deb439868443ad60f07/manifest.json) were read back through connected GitHub; all four Git blob identities match publication. Remote receipt parses to 24 invocations, all assertions passed, exact reviewed head.\n\nproof_and_ci_observed: all 23 check rows returned against total_count23 were inspected; CI's Rust-only feature lane succeeded, Perl/release skipped. Windows advisory subset, wheel build and ub-review were still in progress at observation. Routed Rust Small is Ready-triggered and has not been admitted for this Draft. No skipped lane is called passed.\nreported: author packet's 19 focused tests, check-fast/precommit/traceability, six fixtures and 70 native comparisons; its identity/13 zero-exit receipts and original red log were inspected. This review did not independently repeat that entire matrix.\nproof_or_review_missing: protected integration qualification, actual merge-object checkout, full workspace/golden/dogfood suite, native Windows, nondefault preview/Perl packet runtime, release/package and fanout qualification are not established here.\nblocking_findings: none in the inspected bounded repair.\nnon_blocking_suggestions: none.\nrefuted_or_stale_findings: none; no substantive prior review/thread concerns existed at final read.\naffected_currentness_dimensions: production, stimulus, oracle, public contract, traceability and head reviewed at this exact candidate; later edits require affected-dimension refresh.\nresidual_assumptions_and_non_claims: source and policy constraints preserved; standalone default-feature results do not qualify #8201 or an untested composition.\ndisposition: **REVIEW_INCOMPLETE (semantic checks passed; integration readiness unestablished)**.\n\nNo submitted-source changes, Ready/merge/thread resolution, bot contact, dispatch, release/deploy or security changes. Review-created source checkout was removed after terminal consumers and clean status; local build/evidence retained for recovery. No denials or publication blockers.",
