      "body": "## Exact-head review (`review-pr`)\n\n```text\nreviewed_head_sha: 67dc5af9a15590fc8476d09217232831a0009952\nintegration_basis: e660a99480dc13a4ed93b131042d11506fd484b6 (PR base; current origin/main)\nclaim_boundary: #8210 — under limited_partial_scope, enabled preview advisories must not advertise unselected Python/TypeScript files as analyzed; disabled presence, Perl packet scope, exit 0 for usable partial evidence, and partition semantics stay unchanged.\nchanged_surfaces_and_semantic_owners_inspected:\n  - analysis/pipeline.rs detect_preview_advisories input (producer)\n  - PreviewLanguageAdvisory::analyzed (consumer still file_count>0 / enabled / no non-success run)\n  - JSON/human renderers consume analyzed() unchanged\n  - cli_smoke/partial_preview_disclosure.rs (budget 1/2/3, enabled/disabled, Python+TS)\n  - docs/OUTPUT_SCHEMA.md, RIPR-SPEC-0082, traceability, changelog\nblocking_findings: none on this head\nnon_blocking_suggestions:\n  - analyzed() itself is unchanged; selected-scope is enforced by the path filter so file_count>0 is the ≥1 selected-file gate. A dedicated analyzed() comment would make that contract local, but it is not required for the claim.\nrefuted_or_stale_findings:\n  - CodeRabbit/Gemini quota-limited output is missing review, not a clean result.\n  - Devin “Full review skipped: trial expired” is missing review.\nproof_and_ci_observed:\n  - Local: cargo test --locked -p ripr --test cli_smoke partial_preview_disclosure → 2 passed at this SHA.\n  - Removal challenge in an isolated worktree: dropping the selected-path filter makes python/enabled=true/budget=1 fail with analyzed=true, file_count=2, sample_paths naming src/discount.py and src/extra.py (the original defect).\n  - Hosted draft checks: rust-tests-junit / Ripr Rust Small Result skipped-by-policy (Draft). Advisory lanes that ran are green or skipped-by-policy.\nproof_or_review_missing:\n  - Required merge gate Ripr Rust Small Result has not run on this head (Draft)